      "side": 1,
      "message": "Heh, no, it is not really needed. I originally made this \"cleanup\" as I was going to implement the later patches similarly to Chuanxiao\u0027s v6.15 patchset, where (currently) handle_vmcall() calls pkvm_handle_kvm_call() which is responsible for handling all hypercalls, and doesn\u0027t pass the host vcpu to it. Then I realized that here in v6.12 we can still keep calling __pkvm_init_finalise() and pkvm_reprivilege_vcpu() directly from handle_vmcall() to avoid larger refactoring, so I did that, but didn\u0027t realize that it means that we can also keep passing the vcpu arg to them.\n\nSo I\u0027m happy to abandon these first 2 patches.",
